  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nThe ridge will be centered over Middle TN by the middle of the\nweek with highs continuing to go up a few degrees. We should see \nmid to upper 90s by Wednesday with heat index values as hot as \n107. With the prolonged period of hot temperatures we will see \nmajor heat risk by Tuesday and major to extreme heat risk by \nWednesday. Overnight lows will also be mild throughout the week \nonly falling into the 70s. An upper level trough will push into \nthe Northeast late week into next weekend and that will help to \nflatten the ridge and build it back west but there is some \nuncertainty with that. That will influence if we cool off some or \nnot. With the ridge overhead our rain chances will be little to \nnone for much of the week. Low rain chances enter the forecast \nlate in the week but will be dependent on how the ridge breaks \ndown.",
